{"diagnosis": "Fetch test shows max_addr=0x00000000 with TRAP: no progress vs expected advancing fetches. mem_done at picorv32.v:376-377 is stuck high because trailing `||` lets `!mem_la_firstword` bypass `resetn && mem_xfer && |mem_state` gating, so CPU thinks fetch is done without bus transfer and never issues real mem_valid. Root cause is `)) ||` at picorv32.v:376 which must be `)) &&` to require both transfer-done and firstword handling.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -375,3 +375,3 @@
 	wire mem_busy = |{mem_do_prefetch, mem_do_rinst, mem_do_rdata, mem_do_wdata};
-	wire mem_done = resetn && ((mem_xfer && |mem_state && (mem_do_rinst || mem_do_rdata || mem_do_wdata)) || (&mem_state && mem_do_rinst)) ||
+	wire mem_done = resetn && ((mem_xfer && |mem_state && (mem_do_rinst || mem_do_rdata || mem_do_wdata)) || (&mem_state && mem_do_rinst)) &&
 			(!mem_la_firstword || (~&mem_rdata_latched[1:0] && mem_xfer));
", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), no TRAP: no progress, max_addr advances beyond 0x00000000"}

